                        "text": "~ 2.5 kWh",
                        "icon-filename": "question-email-small.svg"
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "Roughly the same as charging an electric car.",
                        "icon-filename": "question-email-small.svg"
                    }
                ],
                "correct-answer-indexes": [1, 2],
                "after-answer-html": "<span>100 people watching TikTok for 15 minutes equates to 25 hours of total watch time, that amount of watch time (based on <a href='#'>our calculations</a>) corresponds to around 1.5 to 4.5 kWh of energy consumption. In Norway, according to <a href='https://www.elvia.no/smart-forbruk/forbruk-og-sparing/normalt-stromforbruk/'>elvia.no</a>, the average apartment uses roughly 10 899 kWh per year. 10 899 kWh a year is equal to ~ 2.5 kWh every hour.</span><a href='#'><i class='fa-solid fa-book-open'></i>Read more about this subject</a>"
            },
            {
                "name-id": "video-quality",
                "title": "How much more energy does streaming in 4K UHD (2160p) use compared to 720p HD?",
                "description": "",
                "icon-filename": "question-email-big.svg",
                "choices": [
                    {
                        "text": "About the same",
                        "icon-filename": "question-email-small.svg"
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "2—3x more",
                        "icon-filename": "question-email-small.svg"
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "5—10x more",
                        "icon-filename": "question-email-small.svg"
                    },
                    {
                        "text": "30x more",
                        "icon-filename": "question-email-small.svg"
                    }
                ],
                "correct-answer-indexes": [2],
                "after-answer-html": "<h4>The amount of data transfered while streaming grows exponetially based on video quality.</h4><span>A 4K UHD frame consists of ~ 8.3 million pixels, while a 720p HD frame only consists of ~ 0.9 million pixels. 4K offers over nine times as high of a resolution compared to 720p. As a consequence, 4K uses around nine tismes more energy then 720p.</span><a href='#'><i class='fa-solid fa-book-open'></i>Read more about this subject</a>"
            }
